Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:58:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the vsavjw catalogue entry re-pointed to merged-m19
 (14z-170)

jtframe's .rom builder locates every zip member by CRC32 and by nothing else
(mra2rom.go:163-172, no name fallback), so the machine entry must name the
CRCs of the actual build or the MRA produces no .rom at all. Regenerated from
build/m3b_merged27/rompath/vsavjw.zip (sha1 135adb0d) by tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py
in the consuming tree; --check now reports the catalogue matches the build.

EIGHT members moved, and they are the M19 delta exactly:
  vm3j.03d  e703652a -> 0dbc14a6   program: the four ruled #136 fixes (the
  vm3j.04d  2b249a19 -> 02aba291   meter-adder test, the defense rows, the EX-site
  vm3j.07b  ceece3e8 -> b845aef9   branch, the class-0x52 rule), the x2b7ef4
  vm3j.10b  c135afb8 -> 05cdacd0   placeholder repair, and the +0x30 allocator
  vsw.41    c6fe6e5e -> 7102a42c   cascade of the three regrown thunks
  vsw.42    0ed42ee0 -> 7823ef8e
  vsw.33m   bcb4d72c -> 6f5a1c98   group-C glyphs, the M18 -> M19 mark
  vsw.37m   70df1050 -> 60b51461   likewise

No RTL, no cfg, no core change: doc/mame.xml only. cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and
cores/cps15 remain byte-untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TCHcFM32BZhFNXvKqCBLkA
